Chamfers and fillets: a closed chain of lines and arcs whose blend
consumes a face beside it all round (mitcad#300).

The case: a pocket in two steps, its upper wall standing on a ledge as wide
as the chamfer round the deeper part, the wall's foot (four lines and four
arcs) chamfered; or the wall as high as the chamfer too (both faces of the
edges vanish). Two faults:

- SplitKPart: the analytic blend's contact on the ledge, on the ledge's
  boundary, is an unbounded line (ChFiKPart). The hatcher finds domains of
  it where it runs on past the line's ends inside the ledge (beyond the
  corners, where the ledge's edge turns away along the arcs), and
  LineOnBoundary, which recognises a line along the boundary (0148, then
  hatched a little inside, HatchOnBoundary), gave up on unbounded lines: the
  line's pieces were dropped, and walking the gap failed ("Path failed", a
  chamfer's walking not being implemented). LineOnBoundary now looks at an
  unbounded line alongside the spine's edge, from abreast of one of its ends
  to abreast of the other.
- ChFi3d_ContactsAlongFaceEdges: the contacts along the face's edges have
  their ends at the edges' vertices (0148). On a closed stripe the start's
  point had been made before as a point beside that vertex, and ChFi3d_FilDS
  gave the start's interferences the point's index for a vertex's; the
  topological build failed (TopoDS_Builder::Add in
  TopOpeBRepBuild_Builder::MakeEdges). The stripe's points at its start and
  end are now the vertices its contacts end at there.
- IsInput (ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx), asked by SearchFace for those vertices:
  where the spine's tangent stands square to the face's edges at the
  vertex its projection is null, and its angle was measured from a
  direction made of it (a construction error where gp_Dir checks, a
  meaningless angle where it does not). Such a tangent does not run into
  the face.

Upstream: new.
